# Portfolio properties — GBO → BOX — {{BRANCH}} ({{TARGET_ENV}}), reference {{REFERENCE_BRANCH}} ({{REFERENCE_ENV}})

Run date: {{DATE}} · run folder `{{RUN_FOLDER}}` · group: target `{{TARGET_GROUP_PK}}` · GBO source: {{GBO_SOURCE_ENV}} ·
clash mode: {{PP_CLASH_MODE}} · agent `sigom-box-acc-configs-agent` phase 1 (no SQL written) · for the users' review
with `02-acc-gap-matrix.md`.

**How BOX portfolio properties are built** ([ADR 0020](../../../../../docs/decisions/0020-portfolio-properties-imported-from-gbo.md)):
**one BOX property per `Valid` in-scope GBO property** (`InValid` ones are not read, ADR 0014) — its description as
GBO's, its conditions that have a BOX twin (the condition map below; the others dropped), its own topic → account rows
(topics by `CODE`, ADR 0018; internal-list topics → the internal account `INTERNAL`, ADR 0014). The instrument's
local property holds those topics and conditions (built from GBO, not from the reference). Properties whose kept
conditions are identical **clash** — BOX refuses two `Valid` ones (section 3).

**Privacy:** PKs, condition functions, condition values and account codes; property descriptions (run folder only); a
value naming a portfolio, a counterparty or an entity is shown as its hash (`H…`), never the value.

## Summary

| Instrument | GBO properties (Valid, in scope) | BOX properties to create | Held only (mode a) / `InValid` (mode b) | OPEN only | Held and OPEN | Conditions kept / dropped | Topic rows | Account from its GBO property | Internal account |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

Each in-scope property is counted once: to create + held only + OPEN only + held and OPEN = in scope (ADR 0023).
GBO source: {{GBO_SOURCE_ENV}} — the counts, the clashes and the multi-account cases are this source's.

