## 3. Clashes — for the accounting user's choice

A **clash group** = in-scope properties of one instrument (same group, same start date) whose **kept** condition values
are identical (or with no kept condition while another exists): BOX refuses two `Valid` ones (`p_StatusPortFolio`).
The agent recommends none. **Answer:** per group, the GBO property to keep → `decisions.pp_clash_choices` in the
inputs file; the next run (`--from`) creates it.

### Clash group {{K}} — {{INSTRUMENT}} — {{N}} properties

Shared BOX condition values: `{{BOX_CONDITION}}` = {{VALUE}} · …

| GBO property | Description | Its GBO conditions and values (all) | Dropped conditions that told it apart (why it clashes) |
|---|---|---|---|

**Duplicates?** Two properties are duplicates only when every GBO condition value (hashes included) and every topic
→ account row are identical — say so per pair, with that evidence. A rule keeping one is a proposal for the BOX
expert (section 6), never applied before the operator answers (ADR 0023).

What choosing one leaves out — topic → account rows that differ between them:

| List | Topic (`CODE`) | GBO `{{PK_1}}` | GBO `{{PK_2}}` | … |
|---|---|---|---|---|

